  "description": "CexChain protocol objects added in specification revision v0.2, built by an independent Python encoder from spec/cexchain.cddl: a passkey and hardware key registration (actor-set-presence), statements with proof of presence (an Ed25519 WebAuthn assertion; a hardware key's signature over the challenge), a delegation that requires presence, the state commitment (root, proofs, and the log entry that carries it), and a cosign request. All signatures are Ed25519 (deterministic), so every object must be reproduced byte for byte. Keys are throwaway test keys: seed = SHA-256(\"CexChain test key: <name>\").",
